   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation, mitigation, environment and biodiversity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">During the reporting period, Australia&#x2019;s financial contribution to the Pacific Climate Champions program supported the attendance of eight champions at COP28 to amplify the collective Pacific voice on the international stage. 
&#x200d;
Climate Finance &#x2013; Tonga - Hon Sovaleni Hu&#xe1;kameiliku, Prime Minister and Minister for Climate Change 
&#x200d;
Loss and Damage &#x2013; Vanuatu - Hon Ralph Regenvanu, Minister for Climate Change 
&#x200d;
Gender and Social Inclusion &#x2013; Niue - Hon Mona Ainuu, Minister for Natural Resources 
&#x200d;
Adaptation &#x2013; Republic of Marshall Islands - Hon John Silk, Minister for Natural Resources and Commerce 
&#x200d;
Mitigation &#x2013; Samoa - Hon Cedric Schuster, Minister for Natural Resources 
&#x200d;
Just Transition &#x2013; Tuvalu - Hon Seve Paeniu, Minister of Finance and Minister for Climate Change 
&#x200d;
Oceans &#x2013; Fiji - Hon Sitiveni Rabuka, Prime Minister and Minister for Climate Change, and 
&#x200d;
Global Stocktake &#x2013; Cook Islands - Hon Mark Brown, Prime Minister and Minister for Climate Change</narrative>
    </description>
